  "answer": "Project Zenith is a new data analytics initiative launched with a kick-off on June 15th, led by Sarah Tan, with an initial budget of $500,000 for Phase One. The project has since received executive approval for a $2M budget covering all phases. Key milestones include the addition of five new team members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture (onboarding Sept 10), the expansion of the team with Mike Chen and Lisa Ray for machine learning and cloud computing, and the successful completion of the design phase. The project has reached its first major milestone ahead of schedule with a tested prototype for secure file sharing, and is now moving into the development phase led by Omar Jensen, focusing on UI enhancements starting in October. Recent updates highlight a breakthrough in predictive analytics promising to enhance product offerings, with a potential 20% efficiency increase from AI algorithms. Detailed reports and findings are scheduled to be discussed in staff meetings on August 1st, August 5th, and November 20th."
